    "summary": "Man&#039;s gown (boubou, tobe) composed of 139 natural-coloured narrow cotton strips hand-sewn together selvedge to selvedge. Hand woven fron handspun cotton thread. Neck decorated with embroidery, openwork and cutwork in the &#039;two knives (aska biwas) pattern in white on white cotton. Large circle on back of gown embroidered in herringbone stitch with cutwork. Sleeves are hemmed. Neck and bottom edge of garment unhemmed.",
